FIX (a) — guarantee feedback always POSTs. Two layered changes:

1. Add a timeout race + drop cacheBust in diagnostics.ts:
```ts
export async function capturePageScreenshot(): Promise<string | undefined> {
  try {
    const { toPng } = await import("html-to-image");
    const capture = toPng(document.body, {
      cacheBust: false,            // re-fetching every <img> is what hangs
      pixelRatio: 1,
      skipFonts: true,             // avoids cross-origin font CSS fetch stalls
      filter: (node) =>
        !(node instanceof HTMLElement && node.dataset.icSkipCapture === "true"),
    });
    const timeout = new Promise<undefined>((res) => setTimeout(() => res(undefined), 4000));
    return await Promise.race([capture, timeout]);
  } catch {
    return undefined;
  }
}
```

2. Make onSubmit submit-first, screenshot best-effort, so capture is never on the critical path (DiagnosticsPanel.tsx:273-299):
```ts
async function onSubmit() {
  setSaving(true);
  setError(null);
  try {
    const screenshot = await capturePageScreenshot(); // now bounded to <=4s, never rejects
    await submitFeedback({
      phase, verdict,
      snapshot_id: snapshotId, job_id: jobId, project_id: projectId,
      content_hash: decision.content_hash,
      decision_ref: decisionRef(decision),
      comment: comment.trim() || undefined,
      context: decision as unknown as Record<string, unknown>,
      screenshot_data_url: screenshot,
    });
    onSaved();
  } catch (e) {
    setError(e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e));
  } finally {
    setSaving(false);
  }
}
```
The combination of bounded `Promise.race` + `cacheBust:false` is the real fix; submit-first reordering is optional belt-and-suspenders. The timeout is the load-bearing change — keep it even if you keep capture before submit.

FIX (b) — video scene-frame thumbnails. Smallest change that fixes the class: make `_thumb_url` scene-aware and teach the thumb endpoint to serve a scene middle-frame.

Backend diagnostics.py: thread scene_index into the URL. Change `_thumb_url` (diagnostics.py:30-31) to:
```py
def _thumb_url(content_hash: str, scene_index: int | None = None) -> str:
    base = f"/api/media/{content_hash}/thumb.jpg"
    return f"{base}?scene={scene_index}" if scene_index is not None else base
```
Then pass scene at every call site: stage4 (line 110) `_thumb_url(ch, scene)`, stage5 (line 144) `_thumb_url(ch, scene)`, stage6 (line 176) `_thumb_url(ch, scene)`. Cast (line 205) stays photo-only.

Backend media.py: accept the optional `scene` query param and resolve a scene frame:
```py
from fastapi import Query

@lru_cache(maxsize=2048)
def _find_scene_frame(content_hash: str, scene_index: int) -> str | None:
    root = paths.projects_dir()
    if not root.is_dir():
        return None
    for label in ("middle", "start", "end"):
        for match in root.glob(f"*/cache/scenes/{content_hash}/scene-{scene_index}-{label}.png"):
            if match.is_file():
                return str(match)
    return None

@router.get("/{content_hash}/thumb.jpg")
async def get_media_thumb(content_hash: str, scene: int | None = Query(default=None)) -> FileResponse:
    if not _HASH_RE.match(content_hash):
        raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail="invalid content hash")
    if scene is not None:
        frame = _find_scene_frame(content_hash, scene)
        if frame is not None and Path(frame).is_file():
            return FileResponse(frame, media_type="image/png", content_disposition_type="inline")
        _find_scene_frame.cache_clear()
        # fall through to photo thumb (some refs may be mis-tagged), else 404
    path = _find_thumb(content_hash)
    if path is None or not Path(path).is_file():
        _find_thumb.cache_clear()
        raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND, detail=f"no thumbnail for {content_hash}")
    return FileResponse(path, media_type="image/jpeg", content_disposition_type="inline")
```
No frontend change needed — DecisionCard (DiagnosticsPanel.tsx:213-219) already renders `decision.thumb_url`. The `?scene=` PNG will load; the placeholder branch (line 222) becomes the fallback only when a scene frame is genuinely missing.

FIX (c) — quality/narrative/specialness on DROP cards. Root cause: dropped assets aren't in candidate_set.items, and the rank drop carries no scores. Smallest robust fix is to make Stage 4 log the scores it already has on the drop entries, then surface them. Two parts:

Backend stage4_prefilter.py — enrich the drop entries. Add a tiny helper and use it at the two score-less drop sites:
```py
def _scores(a: _Asset) -> dict[str, float]:
    return {
        "quality_score": a.quality_score,
        "narrative_relevance": a.narrative_relevance_score,
        "specialness_score": a.specialness_score,
    }
```
rank_below_target_size drop (line 172-178): `{"key": asset.key, "decision": "drop", "reason": "rank_below_target_size", **_scores(asset)}`. Apply the same `**_scores(asset)` spread to the other drop sites (dedup/semantic-dedup at lines 474, 552, 623, 686 and the quality-floor at 492-499 — floor already has quality_score; add narrative+specialness). Also add `**_scores(asset)` to the keep entry (line 180) so kept cards show scores too.

